cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >
  If you use this synthetic dataset generator in your research, please cite it
  using the metadata below.

title: >
  pad-amp-dispo-synth: A Synthea Module and OMOP ETL Producing a Synthetic CDM of
  Major Lower Extremity Amputation Patients

authors:
  - given-names: "Adam P."
    family-names: "Johnson"
    name-suffix: "MD, MPH"
    affiliation: "Duke University School of Medicine, Department of Surgery"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3014-6372"
  - given-names: "Sasank"
    family-names: "Kalipatnapu"
    name-suffix: "MD"
    affiliation: "University of Massachusetts School of Medicine"
  - given-names: "Ayman"
    family-names: "Ali"
    name-suffix: "MD"
    affiliation: "Duke University School of Medicine, Department of Surgery"

version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-02"

repository-code: "https://github.com/Duke-Vascular-Informatics/pad-amp-dispo-synth"
url: "https://github.com/Duke-Vascular-Informatics/pad-amp-dispo-synth"

license: GPL-3.0

abstract: >
  A data-generation-only repository: a Synthea module and a CSV-to-OMOP ETL that
  produce a fully synthetic OMOP CDM v5.4 dataset of patients undergoing major
  lower extremity amputation for dysvascular, diabetic, or wound indications, with
  a modeled 90-day post-discharge emergency department visit outcome and a
  Veterans Affairs Frailty Index comorbidity burden. It contains no real patient
  data and exists so that downstream OHDSI Strategus study pipelines can be
  developed and verified end to end before any run against real data. It was used
  to develop and verify the pipeline for the non-home discharge risk score
  validation study (pad-amp-nhd-val).
  Funding: Research reported in this publication was supported by the National
  Center For Advancing Translational Sciences of the National Institutes of Health
  under Award Number K12TR005435. The content is solely the responsibility of the
  authors and does not necessarily represent the official views of the National
  Institutes of Health.

keywords:
  - OMOP CDM
  - OHDSI
  - Synthea
  - synthetic data
  - major lower extremity amputation
  - peripheral artery disease
  - clinical informatics
  - R

